* Peavey 5150 (EVH 120 preamp board 81501510, 5-Feb-92), preamp stage 1 of 3: the input, V1A, the Rhythm (clean)
* and Lead (ultra) gain networks selected by the relays, and V1B. Transcribed from the factory drawing.
* Stage 2 (stage2.net) takes V1B's plate through a link source; the V2A input network (C2, R6, R9, R20 / K1B)
* is repeated here as V1B's load.
*
* Relay contacts as drawn (coil off) / energised: K2A, K2B pick the clean (VR1, VR6) or ultra (VR2, VR7)
* pot; K4A puts 470k || 270p (off) or 2.2M || 470p (on) in the clean network and K4B a 39k + 0.1u shunt
* (off) or nothing (on); K1A closes the 22u on V1B's cathode to ground (off) or leaves it behind 47k
* (on); K1B puts 220k to ground on V2A's grid (off) or nothing (on). Jack modes in amp.json:
* Rhythm = all off, Crunch = K4 on, Lead = K2 and K1 on. Which coil states the front panel really gives
* each channel is an assumption: the drawing shows the contacts, not the switching logic.
*
* The V1 rail (node x1) is a fixed source at its idle value (the real one is a 22k + 10k RC from the V3 rail
* with 22u caps: it follows the power supply only over a second or two). x3 is unused in the stages.
* C3, C4, C5 "1A50NP" are read as 1u 50 V non-polar.

V VRAIL x3 100 440
V VX1 x1 50 322
* Guitar, input jack (22k), 39p, 0.1u coupling, 1M grid leak, 68k grid stopper.
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance. RSRC is the plain 7k source: the "Off" setting, and what a pedal in front of the amp
* looks like. A pickup replaces it with its own impedance as seen from the open-circuit voltage (the recording): the
* coil (winding resistance RPU + inductance) in parallel with its winding capacitance CPU and an eddy-current loss resistor
* RPL, then the cable capacitance (200 pF per 2 m, switched in steps of 200, 400 and 800 pF). The engine sets the values:
* single coil = coil 1 (2.5 H), humbucker and P-90 = coil 2 (5 H) with their own resistances; open = 1e12.
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p
R R27 in nin 22k
C C20 nin 0 39p
C C15 nin g1 0.1u
R R25 g1 0 1M
R R22 g1 gv1a 68k

* V1A.
T V1A gv1a p1a k1a 12AX7
R R2 x1 p1a 220k
R R12 k1a 0 1k82
C C3 k1a 0 1u
C C6 p1a p1 22n

* Clean (Rhythm) network: K4A selects the series element, then 1M into the VR1 pot (clean pre).
R SW_K4A3 p1 n19 1
R R19 n19 q 470k
C C51 n19 q 270p
R SW_K4A4 p1 n43 1e12
R R43 n43 q 2M2
C C13 n43 q 470p
R R21 q h 1M
R SW_K4B6 h n23 1
R R23 n23 nc63 39k
C C63 nc63 0 0.1u
C C10 q fl 470p
R R75 fl h 2M2
R SW_S1C fl h 1e12
R VR1_T h w1 1
R VR1_B w1 0 1
C C27 h w1 180p

* Ultra (Lead) network: 470k || 2.2n into the 1M VR2 pot (ultra pre) with its bright 1n and 1M across the top.
R R29 p1 b 470k
C C17 p1 b 2n2
R R41 b 0 1M
R VR2_T b w2 1
R VR2_B w2 0 1
C C19 b w2 1n
R R40 b w2 1M

* K2A: the selected pre pot wiper goes to V1B's grid through 470k.
R SW_K2A3 w1 k2 1
R SW_K2A4 w2 k2 1e12
R R82 k2 gv1b 470k

* V1B with the K1A bass bypass (22u, 47k).
T V1B gv1b p1b k1b 12AX7
R R3 x1 p1b 100k
R R17 k1b 0 1k82
C C4 k1b 0 1u
C C26 k1b kn 22u
R R18 kn 0 47k
R SW_K1A kn 0 1
C C2 p1b a2 22n
R R6 a2 g2a 470k
R R9 g2a 0 1M
R R20 g2a n20 220k
R SW_K1B n20 0 1


* Load of V1B's plate: V2A's input network (stage 2 repeats it behind the link source).
